From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:57:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs: say places' sealed open names its database by a key's
 handle

places_api's new_sealed still said every connection opens the database
by a name that carries the key, which is what patch 0001 did and patch
0005 ended: the name carries a handle to the key, which obfsvfs keeps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../components/places/src/api/places_api.rs                 | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/third_party/application-services/components/places/src/api/places_api.rs b/third_party/application-services/components/places/src/api/places_api.rs
index a9ffddcc60..ac66b3e171 100644
--- a/third_party/application-services/components/places/src/api/places_api.rs
+++ b/third_party/application-services/components/places/src/api/places_api.rs
@@ -199,9 +199,9 @@ impl PlacesApi {
     }
 
     /// As [`PlacesApi::new`], with the database sealed under `key`, 32 bytes: its pages, its write-ahead log and its
-    /// journal are sealed through sql-support's obfsvfs. Every connection opens it by a name that carries the key,
-    /// which is never logged. It is sealed when it is made: a database in the clear, or one sealed under another key,
-    /// is refused, and left as it is.
+    /// journal are sealed through sql-support's obfsvfs. Every connection opens it by a name that carries a handle
+    /// to the key, never the key, which obfsvfs keeps. It is sealed when it is made: a database in the clear, or one
+    /// sealed under another key, is refused, and left as it is.
     pub fn new_sealed(db_name: impl AsRef<Path>, mut key: Vec<u8>) -> Result<Arc<Self>> {
         let db_name = normalize_database_path(db_name)?;
         let sealed = sql_support::obfsvfs::sealed_name(&db_name, &key);
-- 
